The Ministry of Propaganda reports:
[olist]
The Ministry of Foreign Policy looks calm, but in fact the work is humming! In order to increase the influence on the neighboring states, the Ministry:

Added Traditional Chinese (zh-tw), Japanese (ja) and Italian (it);
Improved the translation to Simplified Chinese (zh-cn);


The Ministry of Innovation successfully continues to implement advanced solutions, namely:

Ability to display the current task in the quest log when using the controller;
Optimized logic for choosing cameras and furnishings in the apartment: Up/Down D-Pad – switching between the choice of cameras and furnishings, Left/Right D-Pad – switching between cameras or between furnishings;


The Ministry of Counterintelligence has made tremendous strides in exposing foreign spies. As a result, more than a hundred spies were expelled from our progressive state, and the damage was eliminated. In particular, the Ministry of Damage Elimination has corrected the following errors:

Bug that caused the "Get All" button not to appear when you first opened the desktop;
Bug that caused gamepad control blocking during theft under certain conditions;
Bug due to which, after reassignment, the control remained on the previous keys;
Bug in text scrolling in the log;
Incorrect display of control legend for the controller;
Bug due to which the scrolling of the task list did not work during pause;
Bug due to which it was not possible to scroll the evidence list when using the gamepad;
Bug due to which you could search items in the apartment while the main character was caught red-handed;
Bug due to which the main character could stay in the apartment after he paid off the police;
Bug due to which theft blocked progress in case of conversation with the two policemen;


The Ministry of Self-admiration continues to update the Credits section. Our Wise Leader is seriously considering the possibility of using this section as a census tool in the future because every day the Beholder project is becoming more and more popular!
[/olist]

